<h2>Backups</h2>
<p>HardPoint backs up your shop by itself every night at 2 a.m.: every record, product image and delivery photo, checked file by file after it's stored. Owners find them under <strong>Settings › Your data › Backups</strong>.</p>
<ol>
  <li>To make one straight away, for example before a big price change or a stock take, press <strong>Back up now</strong>. It usually takes a few minutes.</li>
  <li>Choose how often backups run under <strong>Back up automatically</strong>: every day, every week (Mondays), every month (the 1st) or off, and how many to keep under <strong>Automatic backups to keep</strong>. Backups you make yourself are kept for 30 days. Press <strong>Save</strong>.</li>
  <li>Every owner gets an email when a backup is ready. To hear only about problems, choose <strong>Only if one fails</strong> under <strong>Email the owners</strong>. Owners are always emailed if a backup fails, and HardPoint support is told too.</li>
  <li>Press <strong>Download</strong> next to a backup to keep your own copy. It's a ZIP of spreadsheet (CSV) files, like an export, with a <strong>manifest.json</strong> that lists a checksum for every file so you can check the copy is complete.</li>
</ol>
<p>Only owners can make, download or delete backups, and each one is recorded in <strong>Activity</strong>. Backups work while the shop is read-only. Passwords, PINs and API keys are never included. These are your shop's own copies: HardPoint also backs up every shop every hour for its own disaster recovery.</p>

<h2>Exporting everything</h2>
<p>The owner can download all of the shop's data from <strong>Settings › Your data</strong>: products, stock, sales, customers, suppliers, purchases and more, as CSV files (they open in Excel or Google Sheets) in one ZIP file. HardPoint emails a link when it's ready; the link works for 7 days. Export works even while the shop is read-only.</p>

<h2>What HardPoint counts</h2>
<p>To see whether shortcuts such as search and Home's to-do list help, HardPoint counts how many times a day each one is used in your shop.
  It keeps only the numbers: not who used them and not what anyone searched for. The counts aren't part of the export.</p>

<h2>Closing your account</h2>
<p>The owner can close the shop from the same page, confirming with their password. From then on the shop is read-only and only owners can sign in, and <strong>30 days later</strong> its data is deleted for good. Until then an owner can change their mind and cancel the closure from the same page.</p>
<p>Export your data first: once it's deleted, it can't be recovered. HardPoint keeps the invoices it issued to your shop, because tax law requires it.</p>
